@startuml
title CoroScope::launch — task creation and launch policy

start
:Invoke task factory with child CoroScope;
:Allocate coroutine frame and shared completion state;
if (Allocation / state initialization succeeded?) then (yes)
else (no)
  :Return allocation_failure;
  stop
endif

if (Launch mode?) then (Immediate)
  :Run coroutine body inline;
elseif (Async) then (Async)
  if (Executor available?) then (yes)
    :Start task on selected executor;
    if (Executor accepted task?) then (yes)
    else (no)
      :Destroy unstarted coroutine frame;
      :Return enqueue error;
      stop
    endif
  else (no)
    :Destroy unstarted coroutine frame;
    :Return executor_unavailable;
    stop
  endif
elseif (Lazy) then (Lazy)
  :Return task initially suspended;
  :Caller may start or await task later;
endif

:Return task handle / result owner;
:Task executes until completion, cancellation, or suspension;
if (Awaiter registered?) then (yes)
  :Publish result and schedule waiter;
else (no)
  :Publish result for later await;
endif
:Release coroutine frame and scope child ownership;
stop

note right
  Immediate starts inline. Async starts through the selected executor.
  Lazy does not enqueue work during launch. Cancellation is cooperative;
  it does not forcibly interrupt a running coroutine.
end note
@enduml
